## Security Baseline

- Enforce HTTPS in production.
- Keep privileged/service credentials server-side only; never expose secrets to
  client bundles.
- Enforce least-privilege access: each actor may touch only their own data.
- Verify inbound webhook signatures before changing any state.
- Validate all server-side mutation inputs.

Add repo-specific authorization rules (roles, tenancy, row-level security).

## Data and Event Principles

The server (database and authoritative services) is the system of record.
Analytics and client caches are mirrors, not the source of truth for
business-critical state.

Actions that affect money, permissions, identity, compliance, or audit trails
must remain attributable, auditable, and recoverable from server state. Browser
storage is cache only. Durable proof (DB/integration/contract tests) — not
browser-only checks — is what verifies these guarantees.

